course: dictionary
lesson: 960
title: Blowguns and the jungle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blowgun is a long, thin tube. You blow hard into one end, and a small dart shoots out of the other end. «The hunter blew into the blowgun, and the dart flew into the trees.» The words blew and dart are the clues: they tell you what a blowgun does.
explain: Blowguns are linked with hunting traditions in the Amazon rainforest and in Borneo, in South-East Asia. In history and geography lessons you can learn how people there have used them. A blowgun is a real weapon.
explain: In stories, a blowgun adds adventure and jungle danger. Safety matters: real blowguns are weapons, not toys. Never copy them or aim one at anyone.
fact: A blowgun is a long, thin tube used as a weapon or for hunting.
fact: You shoot a small dart by blowing hard into one end of the tube.
fact: «Blowgun» is a noun: a blowgun, blowguns.
fact: Peoples of the Amazon rainforest and of Borneo, in South-East Asia, have hunting traditions that use blowguns.
fact: Real blowguns are weapons, not toys.
exercise: «The hunter blew into the blowgun, and the dart flew into the trees.» What is a blowgun? | A tall tree in the rainforest | *A long, thin tube you blow through to shoot a small dart | A kind of fishing net
exercise: In Borneo, hunters have used blowguns for hunting. What is a blowgun used for? | Carrying water across rivers | Playing music at festivals | *Hunting or as a weapon | Lighting fires
exercise: «The blowgun shot a dart into the tree.» Find and copy the word that tells you the dart was sent out fast. | *shot | into | the | tree
test: What should you remember about real blowguns? | *They are weapons, not toys, so never aim one at anyone | They are only used in stories | They shoot water | They are toys for the playground
test: In stories, what does a blowgun usually add? | *Adventure and jungle danger | Peace and quiet at home | Sweet treats | Cold weather
exam: Which two places are linked with blowgun hunting traditions in this lesson? | London and Glasgow | Scotland and Australia | *The Amazon rainforest and Borneo | The Alps and the Sahara
